Revision history for Ham-RTTY

0.001  2026-10-27
    - Bound receiver working buffers and PDL tone-search projection batches.
    - Acquire from the first half second independently of caller block size.
    - Reject WAV history budgets from metadata before reading PCM data.
    - Measure isolated Perl/PDL peak RSS for reception and sample generation.
    - Publish 30 RAM observations with source/input hashes and repeated ranges.
    - Add five licensed external reception examples and offline comparisons.
    - Retain source hashes, conversion commands and independent-decoder limits.
    - Make CLI quick-start settings consistent and show tone/channel values.
    - Report lenient substitutions for event, WAV and MIDI commands on stderr.
    - Bound default receiver search tones by the actual sample rate.
    - Correct and verify the streaming guide's received-text example.
    - Restore the shared Ham-CW guides, example catalog and runner.
    - Align POD signatures, option lists and architecture notes with Ham-CW.
    - Retain project copyright in README, module POD and NOTICE.
    - Match Ham-CW site footers and guide credits without repeated author names.
    - Align README and documentation navigation with the Ham-CW structure.
    - Add ITU ITA2 and US tables, FIGS/LTRS state and unshift-on-space.
    - Add start-stop events, continuous-phase AFSK and incremental reception.
    - Add protected WAV/MIDI files, RTTY CLI and optional PDL projections.
    - Adapt documentation site, CI and release tooling from Ham-CW.
    - Keep unverified release gates explicit; real recordings remain missing.
